  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Jeremiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 42,
    "summary": "Jeremiah promises Johanan and the remnant of Judah peace and safety if they remain in Judah, but the sword, famine, and pestilence if they go to Egypt.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then all the captains of the forces, and Johanan the son of Kareah, and Jezaniah the son of Hoshaiah, and all the people from the least even unto the greatest, came near,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:1",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And said unto Jeremiah the prophet, Let, we beseech thee, our supplication be accepted before thee, and pray for us unto the Lord thy God, even for all this remnant; (for we are left but a few of many, as thine eyes do behold us:)",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 139,
            "end": 143
          },
          {
            "start": 183,
            "end": 186
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:2",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "That the Lord thy God may shew us the way wherein we may walk, and the thing that we may do.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:3",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Jeremiah the prophet said unto them, I have heard you; behold, I will pray unto the Lord your God according to your words; and it shall come to pass, that whatsoever thing the Lord shall answer you, I will declare it unto you; I will keep nothing back from you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "Num. 21:7; 1 Sam. 7:5; 2 Ne. 33:3; Enos 1:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 59
          },
          {
