                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:5",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Whether it be good, or whether it be evil, we will obey the voice of the Lord our God, to whom we send thee; that it may be well with us, when we obey the voice of the Lord our God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "D&C 25:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 36
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 25:16.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 25:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "doctrineandcovenants",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 25,
                    "end": 25,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:6",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass after ten days, that the word of the Lord came unto Jeremiah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:7",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Then called he Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces which were with him, and all the people from the least even to the greatest,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:8",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And said unto them, Thus saith the Lord, the God of Israel, unto whom ye sent me to present your supplication before him;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:9",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "If ye will still abide in this land, then will I build you, and not pull you down, and I will plant you, and not pluck you up: for I repent me of the evil that I have done unto you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "IE I feel compassion regarding the punishment I bring upon you. JST Jer. 42:10 … and I will turn away the evil that I have done unto you."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 76
          },
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 122
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:10",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Be not afraid of the king of Babylon, of whom ye are afraid; be not afraid of him, saith the Lord: for I am with you to save you, and to deliver you from his hand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 107
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:11",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And I will shew mercies unto you, that he may have mercy upon you, and cause you to return to your own land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:12",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye say, We will not dwell in this land, neither obey the voice of the Lord your God,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:13",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Saying, No; but we will go into the land of Egypt, where we shall see no war, nor hear the sound of the trumpet, nor have hunger of bread; and there will we dwell:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "HEB shofar or alarm."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:14",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And now therefore hear the word of the Lord, ye remnant of Judah; Thus saith the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel; If ye wholly set your faces to enter into Egypt, and go to sojourn there;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 137,
            "end": 142,
            "text": "Jer. 44:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 44:12.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 44:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 44,
                    "end": 44,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:15",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Then it shall come to pass, that the sword, which ye feared, shall overtake you there in the land of Egypt, and the famine, whereof ye were afraid, shall follow close after you there in Egypt; and there ye shall die.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:16",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "So shall it be with all the men that set their faces to go into Egypt to sojourn there; they shall die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence: and none of them shall remain or escape from the evil that I will bring upon them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:17",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "For thus saith the Lord of hosts, the God of Israel; As mine anger and my fury hath been poured forth upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem; so shall my fury be poured forth upon you, when ye shall enter into Egypt: and ye shall be an execration, and an astonishment, and a curse, and a reproach; and ye shall see this place no more.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 231,
            "end": 241,
            "text": "Jer. 44:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 44:12.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 44:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 44,
                    "end": 44,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:18",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord hath said concerning you, O ye remnant of Judah; Go ye not into Egypt: know certainly that I have admonished you this day.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 78,
            "text": "Deut. 17:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Deut. 17:16.",
            "prettyString": "Deuteronomy 17:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "deuteronomy",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 17,
                    "end": 17,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:19",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye dissembled in your hearts, when ye sent me unto the Lord your God, saying, Pray for us unto the Lord our God; and according unto all that the Lord our God shall say, so declare unto us, and we will do it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "HEB have deceived your souls."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 208,
            "end": 211
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Jeremiah 42:20",
        "book": "Jeremiah",
        "chapter": 42,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And now I have this day declared it to you; but ye have not obeyed the voice of the Lord your God, nor any thing for the which he hath sent me unto you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Disobedience."
          }
        ],
